    "df3[\"respiratory_support\"] = df3[\"respiratory_support\"].fillna(\"None\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6342f45a-ac5b-4d19-ade0-ced5d13425cd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "-Respiratory_support being 98% empty doesn't mean 98% of records are broken — it means respiratory support (mechanical ventilation) is a rare intervention, and its absence is itself clinical information. Filling with \"None\" rather than dropping the column preserves that signal."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "bc48eb79-df48-4f86-86d4-8af525995fee",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "time_of_death__days_from_admission: 16 rows flagged '1' but missing a time value\n",
      "readmission_time_days_from_admission: 1 rows flagged '1' but missing a time value\n",
      "time_to_emergency_department_within_6_months: 7 rows flagged '1' but missing a time value\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "checks = [\n",
    "    (\"time_of_death__days_from_admission\", \"death_within_6_months\"),\n",
    "    (\"readmission_time_days_from_admission\", \"re_admission_within_6_months\"),\n",
    "    (\"time_to_emergency_department_within_6_months\", \"return_to_emergency_department_within_6_months\"),\n",
    "]\n",
    "for time_col, flag_col in checks:\n",
    "    mismatch = ((df3[flag_col] == 1) & (df3[time_col].isna())).sum()\n",
    "    print(f\"{time_col}: {mismatch} rows flagged '1' but missing a time value\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5abc1a60-079b-433d-930b-75180a9f1c5d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "-The time-to-event columns (time_of_death, readmission_time, time_to_ED) being mostly empty reflects competing risks structure: most patients simply didn't have the event, so there's no time to record. This is normal in survival data, not a data quality failure."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "4f8e426a-ec56-4549-8901-a97b568b4c20",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df3[df3[\"return_to_emergency_department_within_6_months\"].isna()]\n",
    "df3[\"return_to_emergency_department_within_6_months\"] = (\n",
    "    df3[\"return_to_emergency_department_within_6_months\"].fillna(0)\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ec5ee62e-8596-4e08-8b14-aff96352805e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "-The mismatch checks (16 death-flagged rows with no death time, 7 ED-flagged rows with no ED time) are the real find — these are genuine data entry gaps or logic errors that need manual review before you trust the death/readmission timing analysis. This is different in kind from the structural missingness above."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4b94c2df-e99f-48d6-ba8c-faa2cdf7939b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 4. Fix data types"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "749308b2-9dd1-49e5-be19-dac1562eb6b1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Unparsed dates: 0\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "inpatient_number                                          object\n",
       "destinationdischarge                                    category\n",
       "admission_ward                                          category\n",
       "admission_way                                           category\n",
       "discharge_department                                    category\n",
       "visit_times                                                int64\n",
       "respiratory_support                                     category\n",
       "oxygen_inhalation                                       category\n",
       "dischargeday                                               int64\n",
       "admission_date                                    datetime64[ns]\n",
       "outcome_during_hospitalization                          category\n",
       "death_within_28_days                                       Int64\n",
       "re_admission_within_28_days                                Int64\n",
       "death_within_3_months                                      Int64\n",
       "re_admission_within_3_months                               Int64\n",
       "death_within_6_months                                      Int64\n",
       "re_admission_within_6_months                               Int64\n",
       "time_of_death__days_from_admission                       float64\n",
       "readmission_time_days_from_admission                     float64\n",
       "return_to_emergency_department_within_6_months             Int64\n",
       "time_to_emergency_department_within_6_months             float64\n",
       "dtype: object"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 9,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df3[\"admission_date\"] = pd.to_datetime(df3[\"admission_date\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "print(\"Unparsed dates:\", df3[\"admission_date\"].isna().sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "binary_cols = [\n",
    "    \"death_within_28_days\", \"re_admission_within_28_days\",\n",
    "    \"death_within_3_months\", \"re_admission_within_3_months\",\n",
    "    \"death_within_6_months\", \"re_admission_within_6_months\",\n",
    "    \"return_to_emergency_department_within_6_months\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "df3[binary_cols] = df3[binary_cols].astype(\"Int64\")\n",
    "\n",
    "categorical_cols = [\n",
    "    \"destinationdischarge\", \"admission_ward\", \"admission_way\",\n",
    "    \"discharge_department\", \"respiratory_support\", \"oxygen_inhalation\",\n",
    "    \"outcome_during_hospitalization\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "df3[categorical_cols] = df3[categorical_cols].astype(\"category\")\n",
    "df3.dtypes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "962ceaa9-4e0b-4066-bada-f876db16a70b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "-Casting binary flags to Int64 (nullable) rather than plain int preserves the ability to distinguish \"confirmed 0\" from \"unknown\" if that ever comes up. Casting categoricals lets pandas store and group them efficiently and exposes the full category list at a glance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b8f2d63a-e221-476b-9fa1-d90d54ad7d0d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 5. Check categorical consistency"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "5019dd5b-0ad6-4f38-abe4-4a269e4ddcf7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "destinationdischarge -> ['Died', 'HealthcareFacility', 'Home', 'Unknown']\n",
      "admission_ward -> ['Cardiology', 'GeneralWard', 'ICU', 'Others']\n",
      "admission_way -> ['Emergency', 'NonEmergency']\n",
      "discharge_department -> ['Cardiology', 'GeneralWard', 'ICU', 'Others']\n",
      "respiratory_support -> ['IMV', 'NIMV', 'None']\n",
      "oxygen_inhalation -> ['AmbientAir', 'OxygenTherapy']\n",
      "outcome_during_hospitalization -> ['Alive', 'Dead', 'DischargeAgainstOrder']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "for col in categorical_cols:\n",
    "    print(col, \"->\", list(df3[col].cat.categories))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "70db246e-a7ad-44c8-818d-04d31b438f1a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "-Printing each column's unique categories confirms there's no accidental fragmentation — e.g., \"Home\" vs \"home\" vs \"Home \" being treated as three different discharge destinations. In this dataset it came back clean (4 destinations, 4 wards, 2 admission ways, 3 outcomes), which tells you the source system enforces controlled vocabularies — a good sign for downstream modeling since you won't need fuzzy-matching or recoding."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "341481e5-d893-4e15-8c30-90dcf01ee2d9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 6. Flag outliers for review "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "f77daf36-c9fb-421e-a9e3-1b2d4a611a61",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "visit_times: 148 potential outliers (outside [1.0, 1.0])\n",
      "dischargeday: 163 potential outliers (outside [0.0, 16.0])\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "numeric_cols = [\"visit_times\", \"dischargeday\"]\n",
    "for col in numeric_cols:\n",
    "    q1, q3 = df3[col].quantile([0.25, 0.75])\n",
    "    iqr = q3 - q1\n",
    "    lower, upper = q1 - 1.5 * iqr, q3 + 1.5 * iqr\n",
    "    outliers = df3[(df3[col] < lower) | (df3[col] > upper)]\n",
    "    print(f\"{col}: {len(outliers)} potential outliers (outside [{lower:.1f}, {upper:.1f}])\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f5e3cd6d-006f-470a-ae9d-c0d0fa6f44f2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "-Dischargeday outliers (163 rows outside ~16 days) aren't necessarily errors — a max of 123 days could reflect a genuinely complex, prolonged case (ICU complications, comorbidities). The point of flagging rather than deleting is that in clinical data, extreme values often carry the most important signal (sickest patients), so removing them would bias the dataset toward \"easy\" cases. visit_times outliers (148 rows) flag patients admitted more than once in this dataset — potentially useful as a frailty/chronicity indicator rather than noise."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d682a9c1-d430-400f-82a4-80819826ee2d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 7. Cross-field logic checks"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "fdff7e7d-8aa0-4bd8-907f-f0448b734e5a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "28-day death not reflected at 6 months: 0\n",
      "28-day readmission not reflected at 6 months: 3\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "bad_death = df3[(df3[\"death_within_28_days\"] == 1) & (df3[\"death_within_6_months\"] == 0)]\n",
    "bad_readm = df3[(df3[\"re_admission_within_28_days\"] == 1) & (df3[\"re_admission_within_6_months\"] == 0)]\n",
    "print(\"28-day death not reflected at 6 months:\", len(bad_death))\n",
    "print(\"28-day readmission not reflected at 6 months:\", len(bad_readm))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b49658b7-6c5e-41bc-bafe-468246b814bd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "-The 3 rows where a 28-day readmission isn't reflected as a 6-month readmission are a logical impossibility (6-month window should be a superset of 28-day), not clinical variation. This is the kind of finding pure missing-value or outlier analysis won't catch — it only shows up when you check that the relationships between columns are internally consistent. This is often where real transcription or ETL errors hide."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fab16a30-d1ba-4245-808c-41e7f08cabff",
