      "inpatient_number Data Type: object\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# 1. Convert patient ID to string data type\n",
    "df_rx[\"inpatient_number\"] = df_rx[\"inpatient_number\"].astype(str)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Clean whitespace in drug names\n",
    "df_rx[\"drug_name\"] = df_rx[\"drug_name\"].str.strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify data type change\n",
    "print(f\"inpatient_number Data Type: {df_rx['inpatient_number'].dtype}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9565621f-6c53-4ce9-8dd7-7728f46df291",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Aggregation & Reshaping (Long Format to Wide Format)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Actions:\n",
    "Machine learning models require **one row per patient**. We transform the transactional rows using:\n",
    "1. **Total Prescription Count**: Group by `inpatient_number` to calculate total prescriptions per patient (`total_prescriptions_count`).\n",
    "2. **One-Hot Encoding (Pivot)**: Pivot the 25 exact drug names present in the raw data into binary indicator columns (`1` or `0`).\n",
    "3. **Merge Features**: Combine count and individual drug flags into a unified 1-row-per-patient dataset (**27 columns total**)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0ddddceb-0709-4c73-8226-fae0a75dbeb7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Reshaping from Long Format to Patient-Level Wide Format\n",
    "\n",
    "### Actions:\n",
    "1. **Total Medication Count**: Calculate total number of drugs prescribed to each patient (`total_prescriptions_count`).\n",
    "2. **One-Hot Encoding**: Pivot individual drug names into binary indicator columns (`1` = Prescribed, `0` = Not Prescribed).\n",
    "3. **Class Indicator Encoding**: Pivot therapeutic drug classes into binary flags (`1` = On Class Therapy, `0` = Not On Class Therapy)."
   ]
  },
